; claude: the racing kit (see docs/claude_notes/plan_games.md, "What to
; call them: kits"): what racing games share, on top of the playground
; -- the track as data (Road), and a car driven on it (Car). Used by
; TinyOutRun (pseudo-3D, 2D shapes) and TinyVirtuaRacing
; (polygons); and a car on a flat world with a track of waypoints
; (Topdown), used by TinyMicroMachines and TinyMarioKart (Mode
; 7), and by the ones from above -- TinyGranTrak10, TinySuperSprint,
; TinySupercars and TinySuperOffRoad (its walls, bounces and bumps); and
; that car on ground with a height (Offroad), used by TinyIgnition. A
; private library (only the games use it), installed with elm_playground
; for its API documentation.
(library
 (name kit_racing)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries elm_playground)
)
